# This repository is rooted at the home directory, so the default is to ignore
# EVERYTHING and whitelist only the directories that are meant to be tracked.
# Without this, `git add -A` would stage dotfiles containing credentials
# (.claude.json, .config/, .ssh/, cloud CLI tokens) into a public remote.
#
# To track a new directory, add a matching pair of rules below. Both lines are
# required: the first unignores the directory itself, the second unignores its
# contents.

# Ignore everything by default.
*

# Allow this file itself.
!.gitignore

# --- Whitelisted directories ---

# Obsidian vault
!Downloads/
Downloads/*
!Downloads/2026/
!Downloads/2026/**

# Project repos
!Downloads/Projects/
!Downloads/Projects/**

# --- Exclusions inside whitelisted paths ---

# macOS metadata
.DS_Store

# Node
node_modules/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Environment and secrets, in case one ever lands inside a tracked directory
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Obsidian per-machine UI state; the rest of .obsidian/ (settings, plugins) is fine.
Downloads/2026/.obsidian/workspace.json

# Tickets marked `visibility: private` in their frontmatter. That field keeps them
# off the published board, but git does not read it, and this remote is public.
# Add a line here for every private ticket.
Downloads/2026/Tickets/NZ-10-visa-paperwork.md
